      "published_at": "2026-09-22T14:00:00+00:00",
      "snippet": "Publicly traded companies represent a tiny share of the total number of companies producing crude oil and natural gas in the United States, but they make up a large share of U.S. production. In 2025, publicly traded companies accounted for just 2% of about 12,000 oil and natural gas producers but produced 68% of the crude oil and natural gas in the Lower 48 states.",
      "source": "U.S. EIA Today in Energy",
      "title": "Public companies produce most U.S. crude oil and natural gas",
      "url": "https://www.eia.gov/todayinenergy/detail.php?id=68184"
    },
